// Rate-of-Change Momentum
//
// The oldest momentum measurement there is: price now against price N bars ago. Long while
// the change is positive and turning up.
//
// It is included as a CONTROL. Momentum this plain is the null hypothesis every more
// elaborate trend strategy in this library should have to beat out of sample — and often
// does not.
//
// NOTE, because it cost this file a rewrite: "rising" is `r > r[1]`, NOT `r > sma(r, 5)`.
// `sma` reproduces the chart's running sum exactly, including that a single `na` poisons it
// permanently — and `roc` is `na` for its first 20 bars. `sma(roc(close, 20), 5)` is
// therefore `na` for the WHOLE run, every comparison against it is false, and the strategy
// silently never trades. Feed an averager only a series that is already warm, or use `nz`
// and accept the zeros it substitutes.
strategy("ROC Momentum", overlay = false)

r = roc(close, 20)
rising = r > r[1]

plot(r, title = "ROC", color = color.accent)
plot(0, title = "Zero", color = color.mute, style = style.step)

if crossover(r, 0) and rising
    strategy.entry("roc", strategy.long)

if crossunder(r, 0)
    strategy.close("roc")
